read (the shell builtin): from a regular file, without -n or -t, read 256 bytes at a time and give back what follows
the line with lseek (as bash does), instead of a poll and a read for every byte. A file read line by line in a
shell loop: ~10x faster on a PC; on the Tab5's emulated PC each system call costs ~0.4 ms.

--- a/shell/shell_common.c
